From 36708e0253166e1abe30f634edb9da59907aa77a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Chitaru <cristian.chitaru@windriver.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:30:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] intel-ice: update out-of-tree driver to 2.6.6.8

Update the Intel ICE out-of-tree driver to version 2.6.6.8

- ice 2.6.6.8 was provided by Intel

The 2.6.6.8 new update is an Intel interim debug drop
delivered to investigate the E825 PF VSI rebuild failure (-EIO)
and PHY stall seen under sustained SR-IOV RFC2544 traffic. Over
base 2.6.6.4.1 it adds:
- VF VSI rebuild hardening: a failed VF rebuild is isolated and
  logged instead of cascading across the PF
- flex-pipe fixes: a use-after-free fix and mid-removal guards in
  the profile code
- E825C PHY stuck-state detection with an automatic PHY soft-reset
  recovery path and PHY-to-PHC timestamp-offset handling
- debug instrumentation: new debugfs controls (trigger_phy_soft_reset,
  automatic_phy_soft_reset_enable/_threshold, ptp_read_phy_and_phc_time)
  and an ICE_ADD_PROBES "_probes" build option

Test Plan:
Pass: downloader
Pass: build-pkgs --clean intel-ice
Pass: build image
Pass: boot
Pass: check driver version (modinfo ice / cat /sys/module/ice/version)

Signed-off-by: Cristian Chitaru <cristian.chitaru@windriver.com>
